  {
   "topic": "Mating",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Crimped SZH contacts lock into the ZHR housing by a lance in the housing, which makes them easy to insert. The housing plugs into a shrouded header whose round pins meet a high-force contact. With a top-entry through-hole header the mated pair stands 5.9 mm above the board and is 3.5 mm deep. The ZHR housing also mates with the IDC-type ZR connector."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Through-hole board holes",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Holes are φ0.7 ±0.03 on a 1.5 ±0.05 mm pitch, tolerance not cumulative, layout seen from the component side. Hole sizes are guidelines and depend on board material and drilling; glass-cloth boards may want larger holes. The top-entry row sits 2.2 mm (ref.) from the edge opposite the locking side of a 3.5 mm deep outline; the side-entry row sits 4.6 mm (ref.) from the mating-face edge of a 6 mm deep outline."
  },
  {
   "topic": "SMT land patterns",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Pad pitch is 1.5 ±0.05 mm, not cumulative, layout seen from the component side; the figures are guidelines. SM2 side-entry headers locate with two φ1.1 +0.1/0 boss holes a distance C apart. SM4 headers solder two reinforcement tabs to their own pads at the ends of the row."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering length",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Through-hole headers come with a 2.7 mm tail for 0.6 to 1.2 mm boards or a 3.4 mm tail for 1.6 mm boards."
